      "description": "Project-level payments to governments disclosed by extractive industry companies. The data covers payments related to the extraction of petroleum or mineral resources made by over 700 companies to governments in 150+ countries. This dataset is updated weekly from [resourceprojects.org](https://resourceprojects.org/). Since 2014, the EU, Canada, UK and Norway have passed mandatory disclosure laws that require companies listed in their stock exchanges or operating within them to disclose extractive sector payments disaggregated by project and government agency. Companies disclose this data annually, which is scraped and cleaned and presented here. The data here is made available through [resourceprojects.org](https://resourceprojects.org/).",
